s interruptibly (the signal handlers run while it waits; py-mods-1122)"] [374 58 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [400 2 "// PyOS_InputHook (posixmodule.c, 3.13+): pyi has no C input hook, so none is installed and running it does"] [401 2 "// nothing, 0 (_pyrepl's unix_console asks before each wait for input; queue 287, test_pyrepl)"] [483 3 "// kept, never called: pyi does not fork (subprocess runs children through fork_exec)"] [487 2 "// processes (PY6a: subprocess's module-level names); fork, exec and wait are the OS family's (PY6e)"] [531 3 "// the own process's signal handled before kill returns, as on Linux (PY6f's killSignal, builtins_signal.go)"] [541 1 "// atForkHooks are os.register_at_fork's callables (before, after_in_child, after_in_parent)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[71 30] [94 22] [97 50] [107 23] [118 12] [118 26] [142 29] [213 24] [224 25] [238 30] [263 29] [272 33] [287 30] [301 34] [342 35] [367 50] [432 28] [445 57]]} (go/file "builtins_posix.go" :imports [


